00:02:05.888 --> 00:02:08.058
Well, Monte Carlo simulation, you can

00:02:08.058 --> 00:02:10.099
see a lot of these definitions. What

00:02:10.099 --> 00:02:13.169
you're doing is assigning probability distributions

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.800
to uncertain inputs.

00:02:15.179 --> 00:02:17.618
You're then using the computer to randomly

00:02:17.618 --> 00:02:19.490
sample those distributions,

00:02:19.778 --> 00:02:21.979
get some outcomes, and then analyze those

00:02:21.979 --> 00:02:24.008
results. In layman's

00:02:24.008 --> 00:02:26.099
terms, what it really means is when you have

00:02:26.099 --> 00:02:27.038
a formula,

00:02:27.569 --> 00:02:29.740
and if you kind of think of sales, let's

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:32.278
imagine you have sales that's comprised

00:02:32.278 --> 00:02:34.659
of Division A, Division B, and Division

00:02:34.659 --> 00:02:36.659
C, and there are all sorts of ranges of

00:02:36.659 --> 00:02:37.508
those sales.

00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:39.979
Rather than running through scenarios yourself,

00:02:40.099 --> 00:02:42.580
Monte Carlo simulation runs those scenarios

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:43.189
for you

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.939
and actually gives you the percentages

00:02:45.939 --> 00:02:47.808
or the risks of those outcomes.

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:50.159
So it really quantifies risks

00:02:50.699 --> 00:02:52.500
or really scenario analysis.

00:02:53.278 --> 00:02:55.278
I always think it's interesting to talk

00:02:55.278 --> 00:02:56.939
about where these names came from.

00:02:57.439 --> 00:02:59.758
Monte Carlo simulation actually was invented

00:02:59.758 --> 00:03:01.639
as part of the Manhattan Project.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:04.520
The scientists there were actually using this

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:05.979
approach, random sampling,

00:03:06.479 --> 00:03:08.338
to solve their problems.

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:10.830
And they viewed it as similar to

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:13.020
gambling, which is where the Monte Carlo

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.588
casino comes in, the name,

00:03:14.929 --> 00:03:17.110
and so that's how the name came

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.990
about, hence Monte Carlo.

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:21.550
OK, so why as a CFO

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.469
should you use it, or frankly as someone who's forecasting,

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:27.338
it allows you to plan using odds

00:03:27.338 --> 00:03:29.210
and math, not just your opinion.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.199
Thinking about there's a 24%

00:03:32.199 --> 00:03:34.580
chance we're going to do this as opposed to I think

